A||N||4||Daleford||FRONT BRAKE UPGRADE||||5||
Z||000000||Daleford||10-20-2001||12:04 PM||||Where is the best place to review some text on front brake upgrade for an 86 Fiero.   thanks<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||10-20-2001||12:07 PM||||Grand am brakes seem to be popluar. I personally went with 11.25" vented discs all around.<P>Keep in mind most front brake upgrades are going to require a front hub. The hub is a machined down Fiero rotor with longer studws.<P>Also You will want to get a balancer if you are upgrading the front brakes only , or a cheaper route is to remove the proportioning spring in the distribution block. This gives the rear brakes more bias than stock. <P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-20-2001||08:08 PM||||There's a bunch of stuff in my cave. I've got more comming soon about how the step bore MC works. That type MC is far more complicated than many people think. read the stuff in the service and the upgrade articles.<P>Before "upgrading" the brakes, try the manual rear adjustment procedure in my cave. That procedure can have a significant impact on OE system performance. I wasn't joking in that article. It took a week to fully get used to how much better the brakes on my car are after doing that. Rear caliper adjustment is a major problem in OE Fiero brakes.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Daleford||10-21-2001||10:30 PM||||Thank you Ogre. I have printed your site information and we will study it.<BR> I should mention this is not a stock Fiero. It is a stretched chassis with a complete 4.9 FWD Cadillac powertrain attached. The rear brakes therefore are 93 Cadillac disc! We feel the new rear brakes will overwhelm the front.<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||10-21-2001||10:45 PM||||Baer Brakes makes a kit for late model J-Bodies with 13 inch front and 12 inch rear rotors. Since the rotors have the correct lug pattern already, a crafty person could adapt the kit to their car, or maybe not.||||reg||1
